# How each route reaches each module, and what keeps it there, for the analysis's page (bundle.view):
# solved when the page is made (`esb --view=DIR`), from the analysis's JSON, not by the build. Modules
# are the analysis's numbers. Explained (`why-reached`, `why-needs`), a row is the chain from the
# root to the module, each step one of the fewest.
facts

relation root(module)
# A module imports another (both in the analysis), and a module's kept code reads what another declares.
relation imports(module, target)
relation reads(module, reader)

# What each root reaches through imports, from itself. The import is written first: explaining a
# module, what imports it is found by an index, not by going through all the root reaches.
relation reached(root, module)
reached(R, R) :- root(R) ;
reached(R, D) :- imports(M, D), reached(R, M) ;

# What keeps a module in what a root loads: the root, and every module whose kept code reads what a
# module kept declares.
relation needs(root, module)
needs(R, R) :- root(R) ;
needs(R, D) :- reads(D, M), needs(R, M) ;
